# Ethernet PHY: the stock kernel drives every HT80x PHY through the generic
# PHY path, which is passive and leaves the boot loader's RMII set-up alone.
# We do the same and build no PHY-specific driver:
# - Micrel (KSZ8081, the V1.x boards): 0.7.2 built it and the V1.6A of issue
#   #4 then did not boot; 0.7.3 without it does. Why is not established: the
#   "rmii-ref" clock path does not run (our device tree has no such clock);
#   candidates are its BMCR soft reset undoing the boot loader's reg 0x1F
#   set-up, and its broadcast-disable.
# - Motorcomm: its 6.6 driver knows the YT8511/8521/8531/8531S, not the
#   YT8512H of the HT802 V2.5A, which the generic driver has always driven.
# CONFIG_MOTORCOMM_PHY is not set
# CONFIG_WLAN is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT is not set
# CONFIG_SERIO is not set
# CONFIG_VT is not set
# CONFIG_LEGACY_PTYS is not set
CONFIG_V90LINE=y
CONFIG_MTD=y
CONFIG_MTD_DVF99_QSPI=y
CONFIG_NETCONSOLE=y
CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
CONFIG_DVF99_WATCHDOG=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_DVF99=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_DVF99_CONSOLE=y
# CONFIG_HW_RANDOM is not set
# CONFIG_HWMON is not set
# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
